# SWX_GPU_KEEPALIVE_YIELD=1: stop the keep-alive spin kernel as soon as the game commits.
# The spinner fills only real GPU idle: one short self-calibrated kernel on its own
# queue while the game is submitting. Yield (default on) adds a shared stop word the
# kernel polls every 1024 iterations (~25 us); swx_keepalive_game_commit() sets it
# before each main command-buffer commit (normal path and sub_cut), and the last
# completion signals a semaphore the spinner waits on instead of polling every 2 ms.
# Stopped kernels never recalibrate the length. =0 keeps the old behavior (kernels
# run to their end, 2 ms polling) for A/B. Start moved to the first mtl_sub_begin
# (every submit stamps activity, monotonic CLOCK_UPTIME_RAW); the 100 ms idle stop
# is unchanged. No yield message and no stop write with keepalive off (the stop
# buffer doubles as the spinner-exists guard). Aggregate counters only (power-line
# log: kernels, GPU ms, max ms, stopped, stop-callback max wall clock which includes
# CPU scheduling and is not a kernel-exit proof; no per-kernel logging). Gate
# approval uses kernels, GPU ms, max ms and stopped (MNG parity). A/B via
# ab_test.py keepalive|yield.
